Per Apache License 2.0, Section 4(b), the following changes have been made
to the original work:

- Fixed tide prediction sensor going unavailable nightly between midnight
  and the first tide of the day, caused by a prediction window that could
  start after every tide in range (api_clients/noaa_api_client.py).
- Guarded against unavailable "following tide" data cascading into loss of
  all other tide attributes.
- Fixed barometric pressure sensor reporting millibars mislabeled as inches
  of mercury, producing values off by a factor of ~33.86
  (sensors/noaa_sensors.py).
- Added optional datum correction: applies NOAA's published monthly mean
  sea level offset to tide prediction levels, correcting for sea-level rise
  and seasonal variation since the 1983-2001 tidal epoch. Off by default;
  enabled via integration options.
- Rebranded package metadata (manifest.json, documentation and issue
  tracker links) to point at the netFusion-Solutions fork.

The bug fixes above have also been submitted upstream as pull requests to
Flight-Lab/HA_Noaa_Tides. The datum correction feature is fork-specific and
is not part of those submissions.
